There was a BBS system in the early 80s I belive called King of the Mountain. 
It was a very simple message only BBS set in a medival style menu and what not.
The thing that made it interesting was that the program had a small grammar
checker type of subroutine that would analyze every message posted for content.
If your message had goo content (long words, good average word and settence length, a few other things found in many modern grammar checkers) you would be
awarded points. They were like our very own nethack exp. points. The more you
posted to the BBS and the better the quality of messages, the more exp.
Eventually you would start to go up levels on the BBS. As you went up you were afforded more abilities, such as changing your name in posts and posting 
anonymously. I don't remmber the specifics but at high levels you had control
of very low level messages and could alter thier time stamps and other nasty
diety level like things. Was a really great BBS. If ANYONE can find this and 
